{"title":"Career Roadmap — Product Design Engineer","role":"Product Design Engineer","summary":"A Product Design Engineer converts product requirements into manufacturable physical products by combining engineering principles, CAD, materials, manufacturing, simulation, prototyping and design-for-manufacture.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Tech / B.E.","Course":"Design Engineering / Engineering Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Product Design Engineer converts product requirements into manufacturable physical products by combining engineering principles, CAD, materials, manufacturing, simulation, prototyping and design-for-manufacture."},{"type":"p","text":"The role can span:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Consumer products"},{"text":"Automotive components"},{"text":"Industrial machinery"},{"text":"Electronics enclosures"},{"text":"Medical devices"},{"text":"Robotics"},{"text":"Aerospace components"},{"text":"Appliances"},{"text":"Energy equipment"},{"text":"Industrial tooling"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A strong Product Design Engineer is not just a CAD operator. They should be able to move through:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Requirement","Concept","Engineering Design","CAD","Simulation","Prototype","Testing","Manufacturing","Product Improvement"]}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Period","Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"2026–2030"},{"text":"B.Tech/B.E."},{"text":"Engineering fundamentals, CAD, materials and manufacturing"}],[{"text":"2030–2033"},{"text":"Design Engineer / Graduate Engineer Trainee"},{"text":"CAD, drawings, prototyping and design changes"}],[{"text":"2033–2037"},{"text":"Product Design Engineer"},{"text":"Independent component/product development"}],[{"text":"2037–2041"},{"text":"Senior Product Design Engineer"},{"text":"Complex products, simulation and design leadership"}],[{"text":"